xvfb-static: advertise an XI2.1 ScrollClass on the core pointer

Grows the core pointer from 2 valuator axes to 4 and marks the two new axes
as scrolling:

  SetScrollValuator(pDev, 2, SCROLL_TYPE_HORIZONTAL, 120.0, SCROLL_FLAG_NONE);
  SetScrollValuator(pDev, 3, SCROLL_TYPE_VERTICAL,   120.0, SCROLL_FLAG_PREFERRED);

Without a scroll-marked axis, scroll can only be expressed as core wheel
buttons 4/5/6/7, which carry a button number but no magnitude, so every
scroll is quantised to exactly one detent. dix/getevents.c's
wheel-button-to-scroll conversion is already present in this tree and needs
only an axis marked as scrolling; no other file requires changes.

Ordering within CorePointerProc: the two SetScrollValuator calls must run
after InitPointerDeviceStruct returns, never before. InitPointerDeviceStruct
calls InitValuatorAxisStruct for every axis, and InitValuatorAxisStruct ends
with SetScrollValuator(dev, axnum, SCROLL_TYPE_NONE, 0, SCROLL_FLAG_NONE)
(Xi/exevents.c), which silently clears any scroll marking already set on that
axis -- no error, no log line, the class is simply absent from XIQueryDevice
output at runtime.

CorePointerProc, not hw/vfb/InitInput.c's vfbMouseProc: both compile, and
both would show a scroll class in a device listing, but only CorePointerProc's
device is the one XTEST-injected input reaches. CorePointerProc builds the
"Virtual core XTEST pointer" slave, via AllocDevicePair(..., CorePointerProc,
CoreKeyboardProc, ...) in InitCoreDevices immediately below in this file;
vfbMouseProc builds an unrelated "Xvfb mouse" device XTEST never targets. The
class also belongs on the slave rather than the master: a client tracking the
master's lastSlave sees a DeviceChanged(SlaveSwitch) if motion and scroll
arrive from different slaves, which invalidates the first event of a burst.

increment is 120.0 and is a wire contract, not a free parameter. One legacy
wheel click moves the axis by exactly one increment, so a client can scale
injected valuator units and legacy clicks identically. Changing it changes
the meaning of every injected delta.

SCROLL_FLAG_DONT_EMULATE is deliberately not set on either axis. Setting it
stops the server emitting buttons 4/5/6/7 for scroll motion, which breaks
every client predating XI2.1. test/xi2-scroll-check.c check b pins this.

Applies to all three build variants: dix/devices.c is core server code, not
GLX-specific. Ordering relative to xserver-0001 through 0005 is free -- this
patch touches only dix/devices.c, while 0001 through 0004 touch xkb/ and 0005
touches glx/.

--- a/dix/devices.c
+++ b/dix/devices.c
@@ -660,7 +660,7 @@
 CorePointerProc(DeviceIntPtr pDev, int what)
 {
 #define NBUTTONS 10
-#define NAXES 2
+#define NAXES 4
     BYTE map[NBUTTONS + 1];
     int i = 0;
     Atom btn_labels[NBUTTONS] = { 0 };
@@ -683,6 +683,8 @@

         axes_labels[0] = XIGetKnownProperty(AXIS_LABEL_PROP_REL_X);
         axes_labels[1] = XIGetKnownProperty(AXIS_LABEL_PROP_REL_Y);
+        axes_labels[2] = XIGetKnownProperty(AXIS_LABEL_PROP_REL_HWHEEL);
+        axes_labels[3] = XIGetKnownProperty(AXIS_LABEL_PROP_REL_WHEEL);

         if (!InitPointerDeviceStruct
             ((DevicePtr) pDev, map, NBUTTONS, btn_labels,
@@ -697,6 +699,10 @@
         pDev->last.valuators[0] = pDev->valuator->axisVal[0] + scr->x;
         pDev->valuator->axisVal[1] = scr->height / 2;
         pDev->last.valuators[1] = pDev->valuator->axisVal[1] + scr->y;
+
+        /* xvfb-static: advertise an XI2.1 ScrollClass (see patch header). */
+        SetScrollValuator(pDev, 2, SCROLL_TYPE_HORIZONTAL, 120.0, SCROLL_FLAG_NONE);
+        SetScrollValuator(pDev, 3, SCROLL_TYPE_VERTICAL, 120.0, SCROLL_FLAG_PREFERRED);
         break;

     case DEVICE_CLOSE:
